# ~/.zshenv -- read by EVERY zsh: interactive shells, scripts, and any
# subprocess a program spawns. Keep it to things that genuinely must exist
# everywhere, because everything here is inherited by everything else.

. "$HOME/.cargo/env"

# Machine-local values that are not tracked in this repo -- API keys and the
# like. See zsh/README.md.
#
# Sourcing secrets from here rather than .zshrc means every process inherits
# them, which is not ideal; it is done this way only because that is where
# they already were, and moving them to interactive-only risks breaking a
# script that quietly depends on one. Prefer fetching from the macOS keychain
# on demand, or direnv per project, over adding anything new to this file.
[ -f "$HOME/.zshenv.local" ] && . "$HOME/.zshenv.local"
